// Title: Potential APT-C-12 BlueMushroom DLL Load Activity Via Regsvr32
// Sigma ID: bd70d3f8-e60e-4d25-89f0-0b5a9cff20e0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Tim Shelton, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-02 | Modified: 2023-03-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.010
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects potential BlueMushroom DLL loading activity via regsvr32 from AppData Local
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EF3yLGoWkAEGeLa?format=jpg
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2019/TA/APC-C-12/proc_creation_win_apt_aptc12_bluemushroom.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "regsvr32" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\Local\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll" and ProcessCommandLine contains ",DllEntry"
